  <data name="AbtTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>About Prosary</value></data>
  <data name="AbtTagline.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>A companion for praying the Rosary and other Catholic devotions.</value></data>
  <data name="AbtTypefacesHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Typefaces</value></data>
  <data name="AbtTypeFrank.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — SIL Open Font License 1.1 — Hebrew prayers.</value></data>
  <data name="AbtTypeShofar.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — GPL v2 with font-embedding exception — Hebrew Scripture (Culmus Project, Yoram Gnat).</value></data>
  <data name="AbtTypeAmiri.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — SIL Open Font License 1.1 — Arabic prayers.</value></data>
  <data name="AbtTypeScheherazade.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — SIL Open Font License 1.1 — Arabic Scripture (SIL).</value></data>
  <data name="AbtTypeCardo.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — SIL Open Font License 1.1 — Latin/English Scripture (David J. Perry).</value></data>
  <data name="AbtTypeFooter.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Latin-script prayers use Cambria, which ships with Windows — not bundled with the app.</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMysteryHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Mystery Illustrations</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMysteryIntro.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>All 20 mystery images are classical paintings in the public domain (artist deceased over 100 years), sourced from Wikimedia Commons.</value></data>
  <data name="AbtOtherHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Other Images</value></data>
  <data name="AbtStationsHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Stations of the Cross Illustrations</value></data>
  <data name="AbtStationsFugel.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>All 14 stations: Gebhard Fugel (1863–1939), Kreuzweg (1921), St. Antonius, Bad Saulgau — public domain; photographs by Andreas Praefcke, released into the public domain.</value></data>
  <data name="AbtStationsScriptural.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The scriptural (St. John Paul II) form adds: The Kiss of Judas — Giotto (Scrovegni Chapel, c. 1305); Christ before the High Priest — Gerrit van Honthorst (c. 1617), National Gallery, London; The Denial of St Peter — Rembrandt (1660), Rijksmuseum; Le Coup de Lance — Peter Paul Rubens (1620), Royal Museum of Fine Arts Antwerp — all public domain. Its other scenes reuse illustrations listed elsewhere on this page.</value></data>
  <data name="AbtViaLucis.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Via Lucis scenes: The Disciples at the Tomb — Eugène Burnand (1898), Musée d'Orsay; Noli me tangere — Fra Angelico (San Marco, c. 1440); The Road to Emmaus, the appearances to the apostles, at Lake Tiberias, and in Galilee — Duccio di Buoninsegna (Maestà, 1308–1311), Siena; Supper at Emmaus (1601) and The Incredulity of Saint Thomas (1601–1602) — Caravaggio; Christ's Charge to Peter — Raphael (c. 1515), Royal Collection; The Virgin in Prayer — Sassoferrato (1640–1650), National Gallery, London — all public domain. Its other scenes reuse the Rosary's glorious-mystery illustrations.</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCrownHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Franciscan Crown Illustration</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCrownMagi.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Adoration of the Magi: Bartolomé Esteban Murillo (c. 1655–60), Toledo Museum of Art — public domain. The other six Joys reuse the Rosary mystery illustrations above.</value></data>
  <data name="AbtSorrowsHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Seven Sorrows Illustrations</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMercyHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Divine Mercy Illustration</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMercyBody.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Eugeniusz Kazimirowski, Divine Mercy (“Jezu, ufam Tobie”, 1934), Divine Mercy Sanctuary, Vilnius — the original image painted under St. Faustina’s direction; public domain.</value></data>
  <data name="AbtJpHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Jesus Prayer Illustration</value></data>
  <data name="AbtJpBody.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Christ Pantocrator: encaustic icon (6th century), Saint Catherine’s Monastery, Mount Sinai — the oldest surviving icon of Christ Pantocrator, honoring the prayer’s Eastern tradition; public domain.</value></data>
  <data name="AbtScriptureHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Scripture Sources</value></data>
  <data name="AbtScriptureBody.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Scripture quotations use the Douay-Rheims Bible (English), the Clementine Vulgate (Latin), Franz Delitzsch's Hebrew New Testament translation (sourced from kirjasilta.net/ha-berit) with Hebrew Old Testament passages following the Masoretic text, the Jesuit Arabic Bible (Beirut, 1880, revised 1988), the Russian Synodal Bible (1876), and Ang Dating Biblia (Tagalog, 1905) — all public domain.</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys01Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Annunciation</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit01.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Fra Angelico (d. 1455)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys02Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Visitation</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit02.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Mariotto Albertinelli (d. 1515)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys03Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Holy Night</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit03.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Antonio da Correggio (d. 1534)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys04Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Presentation at the Temple</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit04.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Andrea Mantegna (d. 1506)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys05Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Christ Discovered in the Temple</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit05.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Simone Martini (d. 1344)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys06Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Baptism of Christ</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit06.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Piero della Francesca (d. 1492)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys07Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Wedding at Cana</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit07.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Paolo Veronese (d. 1588)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys08Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Sermon on the Mount</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit08.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Cosimo Rosselli (d. 1507)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys09Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Transfiguration</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit09.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Raphael (d. 1520)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys10Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Last Supper</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit10.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Leonardo da Vinci (d. 1519)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys11Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Agony in the Garden</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys12Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Flagellation of Christ</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit11.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Caravaggio (d. 1610)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys13Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Crowning with Thorns</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys14Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Christ Carrying the Cross</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit12.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Titian (d. 1576)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys15Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Christ Crucified</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit13.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Diego Velázquez (d. 1660)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys16Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Resurrection</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys17Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Ascension of Christ</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit14.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Rembrandt (d. 1669)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys18Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Pentecost</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit15.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — El Greco (d. 1614)</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys19Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Assumption of the Virgin</value></data>
  <data name="AbtMys20Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Coronation of the Virgin</value></data>
  <data name="AbtOther01Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Crucifix</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit16.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Cimabue (d. 1302).</value></data>
  <data name="AbtOther02Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Small Cowper Madonna</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit17.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Raphael (d. 1520).</value></data>
  <data name="AbtOther03Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Faith, Hope, and Charity</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit18.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Raphael, Baglioni altarpiece predella (d. 1520).</value></data>
  <data name="AbtOther04Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Praying Hands</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit19.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Albrecht Dürer (d. 1528).</value></data>
  <data name="AbtOther05Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Holy Trinity</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit20.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Masaccio (d. 1428).</value></data>
  <data name="AbtOther06Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Christ in Limbo</value></data>
  <data name="AbtCredit21.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value> — Fra Angelico (d. 1455).</value></data>
  <data name="AbtOther07Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Michael</value></data>
